 "observations": [
  "The first page of the index, p. [249], without a page number (the contents, p. [III], JP2 0007, give pp. 249-255). The heading «Namen- und Sachregister.» (L01) is centred in the sans-serif type of regular weight of the heading «Glossar.» (p. [241], JP2 0275), with a short rule below it. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr., 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.» on the left and the sheet number «32» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line.",
  "Below the heading the index runs in two columns divided by a vertical rule; transcribed column by column: the left column L02-L39, the right L40-L77. The letter head «A.» (L02) is set in bold, centred in the left column. Each entry begins at the edge of its column, its further lines indented; the subentries that begin with a dash («— domorum», L15; «— plani», L43) are indented less than the further lines. Arabic numerals are the pages of the text and the commentary, roman numerals those of the foreword and the introduction, «T.» the tables and «N.» the footnotes. Words in italics: «Hidjra» (L18), «acofra» (L24), «Heza» (L59); the Greek «ἀναπλήρωσις» (L38) in the slanted Greek type of the edition.",
  "The semicolons of L19, L20 (three), L22 (two), L23, L24, L25, L46 and L53 stand after a thin space (7-13 px); written with a space. L53 is set close («desselben,2—4,34—36 ;Auffindung»), the spaces after the commas and the semicolon 9-13 px; written with ordinary spaces. The dashes are long (30-38 px). L10: a speck below the second a of «Adam»; L20: a speck below the e of «Diocletiani»; not transcribed. L33: «Alexander» stands after «Alienatio», out of the alphabetical order of the index.",
  "Checked against the text, for example: «Abacus» on p. X (JP2 0014), «ʿAbbās b. Saʿīd al-Djauharī» on p. 32 (JP2 0064), «Abraham b. ʿEzrā» on pp. 41, 51 and 99, «Abū’l-Ḥasan ʿAlī» of Morocco on p. 71 (JP2 0103), «Abū Isḥāḳ al-Naḳḳāsh» in the additions, p. 236 (JP2 0268), «Abū’l-Wefā» on pp. 77-78, «Adiectiones» on p. XVIII (JP2 0022), «aequans» on pp. 47, 48, 50 and 233, «nychthemerōn» on p. 80 (JP2 0112), the eras of p. XVI (JP2 0020), «Aḥmed b. al-Muthannā» on p. 51 (JP2 0083), «Albohazen» and «Albumasar» on p. 105 (JP2 0137), «Alienatio» on pp. 103-104 (JP2 0135-0136) and in Tab. 116 (p. 231, JP2 0263), «Almagesti» on p. XI and in Ms. N's addition on p. 16, «ἀναπλήρωσις» on p. 88 (JP2 0120), «Andersen» on p. VI (JP2 0010), «anni vagi» on p. 38 (JP2 0070), «Antiochia» on pp. 83, 95 and 96, «ratum» on pp. 25 and 84, «Arkand» and «Khaṇḍakhādyaka» on p. 79 (JP2 0111), «Āryabhaṭṭa» on p. 42 (JP2 0074), the ascensional difference on pp. 74-76 (JP2 0106-0108). The word «Apsidenlinie» is printed on p. 64 (JP2 0096, L33), and p. 65 (JP2 0097, L11) speaks of the motion of the apsides."
 ],
